Third-party notices for Anole
=============================

Anole is MIT-licensed (see LICENSE). It is built from the components below.
The packages in part A are fetched by `zig build` from the pinned URL in
build.zig.zon, not vendored. Most keep their own licence file, but the zio
package ships no LICENSE (its build.zig.zon .paths leave it out), so this
file carries its notice: the copyright line in part A and the MIT text in
part C. Files in this repository that adapt third-party code carry an
attribution header and are listed in part B; that includes the HTTP core
(src/http/core, adapted from dusty) and the llhttp sources inside it.

Which components end up in a binary depends on the build flags:
`-Dprofile=minimal` links only zio, the HTTP core and llhttp;
`-Dtls=boringssl` adds BoringSSL; `-Dhttp2` adds nghttp2; `-Dhttp3` adds
ngtcp2 and nghttp3; `-Dbrotli` adds Brotli; `-Dkafka` adds lz4; `-Dpostgres` adds pg.zig and
buffer.zig; `-Dsqlite` adds SQLite and zig-sqlite.


